ues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nIn 4.5.stable.mono.official.876b29033, a series of changes in the Camera2D node cause an integer overflow in the bounds checking.\n\nI was using 4.4.1 before, where the problem was not present.\n\n### System information\n\nUbuntu, 4.5.stable.mono.official.876b29033\n\n### Issue description\n\nAs a result, if I create a new camera with \n\n```\nlimitLeft = -2^31\nlimitRight = 2^31 - 1\n```\n\nthe camera is stuck at 0/0.\n\nThe problem likely comes from the line at https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blame/4219ce91f2d1fae65f289d27284a1ab35e9b7b5f/scene/2d/camera_2d.cpp#L229C18-L229C18 , which rewrote the condition logic.\n\n**Expected behavior**\n\nSince the camera limits are integers, I expect int.Max (`2^31 - 1` ) and int.Min (`-2^31`) to be valid limits. Godot uses magic constants here (the defaults are -10000000 and 10000000), but especially when I'm setting limits from code, I'll use int.max and int.min to avoid arbitrary constants.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* create a camera\n* set its limitLeft to a large negative number, e.g. -2^31\n* set its limitRight to a large positive number, e.g. 2^31-1\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[camera-overflow-mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22883979/camera-overflow-mrp.zip) (move with left & right arrow keys)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com